This is on a 500 MHz Celeron box with 128 MB of ram running kernel
2.4.23 with a modified quota patch from patch-o-matic and iptables1.2.9.

Am having this crash repeatedly when the system is acting as a gateway
for one box that uses ftp with a transfer rate at around 2 Mbps.

The attachment enclosed includes the modified 'ipt_quota' files, the
kernel config file, a few other ksymoops and the System.map

Of the ksymoops outputs enclosed the second one let to a kernel crash
while in the other cases the system as a whole hasn't gone down.

On some servers in production that perform similar tasks, the kernel has
been crashing on and off with a lot of junk in any log file that is
being written to at the time. In these cases there aren't any messages
from the kernel. On servers with ext3, an ext3 BUG was being reported in
the kernel logs, but with reiserfs the crash is silent with, as
mentioned earlier, junk characters and portions of other files on the
disk in log files.

Can someone please let me know if this is a known issue?
Any pointers to the possible cause would make my day.

Please do let me know if any other details of the system's configuration
are needed.

